---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import berkeley from "../../img/Busby-Berkeley-Footlight-Parade.jpg"
import CentredImage from "../../components/CentredImage.astro"
import ball_wave from "../../img/unity/ball-wave.png"
---
<Slide t1="Choreography">
    <CentredImage src={ berkeley } size={ [700, 400] } />
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Choreography">
    <ul>
        <li>To produce animated movement, position objects in the <code>Update</code>
            method rather than <code>Start</code></li>
        <li>Use <code>Time.deltaTime</code> to keep movement constant regardless
            of frame rate</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Exercise: Move the Cube">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Make one of the cube examples move <em>periodically</em>
            over time (use sine or cosine)</li>
        <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Translation: easy</li>
            <li class="fragment">Resizing: easy</li>
            <li class="fragment">Rotation: harder</li>
        </ul>

        <li class="fragment">Can you move <em>just part</em> of the cube?</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Making Waves">
    <p>Simple Harmonic Motion</p>

    <CentredImage src={ ball_wave } size={ [750] } />

</Slide>

<Slide t2="Code">
    <div class="text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="csharp" height="475px">
            { `
Vector3 position_wave(int index, float time) {
    const float X_DISTANCE = 0.5f;
    const float Y_DISTANCE = 1.5f;

    float phase = index + time;

    return new Vector3(X_DISTANCE * (index - (NUM_SPHERES - 1) / 2),
                       Y_DISTANCE * (float) Math.Sin(phase),
                       0);
}

void Update()
{
    theTime += Time.deltaTime;

    for (int i = 0; i < NUM_SPHERES; i++) {
        GameObject ga = spheres[i];
        ga.transform.position = position_wave(i, theTime);
    }
}
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Parameterisation">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">This animation is completely fixed</li>
        <li class="fragment">What parameters can be altered?</li>

        <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Identify them one by one</li>
            <li class="fragment">Add them as public variables so that you can
                alter them inside Unity
            </li>
        </ul>

        <li class="fragment">Extra: what about <code>Z</code> dimension?</li>
        <li class="fragment">Extra: what about colour?</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>
